{"seq":82,"slug":"software-supply-chain-security","title":"软件供应链安全","stage":"DONE","category":"cs-fundamentals","chapterCount":4,"docCount":12,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/software-supply-chain-security","rating":{"composite":3.72,"verdict":"stable","groups":{"quality":3.6,"coverage":3.75,"positioning":3.5,"strategic":4},"weights":{"quality":0.3,"coverage":0.25,"positioning":0.2,"strategic":0.25},"profile":null},"introHtml":"<h1 id=\"软件供应链安全\">软件供应链安全</h1><p>二十年前，&quot;软件安全&quot;几乎等同于&quot;我写的代码安全吗&quot;。今天的现实是：一个中等规模的服务，自己手写的代码往往不到 5%，其余九成以上来自第三方依赖、基础镜像、构建工具、CI 插件与包管理器。攻击者很早就看懂了这笔账——与其费力攻破你层层设防的生产环境，不如去污染那条把代码送进你环境的&quot;传送带&quot;。这条传送带，就是软件供应链。</p>\n<p>供应链攻击之所以可怕，在于它的杠杆效应：攻陷一个上游节点，就能一次性污染成千上万个下游用户。SolarWinds 事件中，攻击者篡改的不是某个客户的服务器，而是 Orion 的构建系统，于是带毒更新经由官方签名渠道分发给约一万八千家机构；xz 后门则差一点把一段隐藏的 SSH 远程执行能力，通过一个被社工夺权的开源维护者，植入几乎所有主流 Linux 发行版。这两起事件分别代表了供应链攻击的两种典型形态：攻破企业内部构建流程，与渗透开源协作信任。</p>\n<p>本 hub 用四章，沿着&quot;理解威胁 → 管住依赖 → 证明完整 → 落地工程&quot;的主线层层递进。</p>\n<p>第一章&quot;基础&quot;打地基：先建立完整的威胁面模型，搞清楚攻击者究竟能从哪些环节切入；再用 SolarWinds 与 xz 两个标志性案例把抽象威胁还原成具体的攻击链；最后引入 SLSA 与 S2C2F 这两套成熟度框架，给出&quot;我们现在处于哪一级、下一步该补什么&quot;的统一坐标系。</p>\n<p>第二章&quot;依赖安全&quot;处理最高频的风险来源——你引入的每一个第三方包。它讲清楚依赖投毒、抢注、混淆攻击的原理，引入软件物料清单 SBOM 作为&quot;知道自己用了什么&quot;的前提，再用漏洞扫描与 SCA 把这份清单与已知漏洞数据库对接起来。</p>\n<p>第三章&quot;完整性&quot;回答一个更根本的问题：你拿到的制品，真的是你以为的那个吗？制品签名（以 Sigstore 为代表）证明&quot;谁发布的&quot;，来源证明与构建溯源证明&quot;它是怎么造出来的&quot;，可重现构建则用&quot;任何人重新构建都能得到逐字节相同的结果&quot;为完整性提供最硬的数学保证。</p>\n<p>第四章&quot;工程实践&quot;是收口：把前三章的理念固化进安全流水线与 CI 加固，用策略执行与准入控制让&quot;不达标就不准上线&quot;成为自动化的硬约束，最后用供应链事件响应处理&quot;防线终究被突破之后&quot;的局面。</p>\n<p>四章之间环环相扣：没有第一章的威胁认知，后面的防护就是无的放矢；没有第二章的依赖可见性，第三章的完整性保证就缺了对象；没有第三章的可验证信任，第四章的策略闸门就无据可依。读完全 hub，你会获得一套可落地的纵深防御心智模型，而不是一堆零散的工具名词。</p>\n","chapters":[{"seq":1,"slug":"foundations","title":"基础","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/software-supply-chain-security/foundations","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"supply-chain-threats","title":"软件供应链的威胁面","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/software-supply-chain-security/foundations/supply-chain-threats"},{"seq":2,"slug":"attack-case-studies","title":"典型攻击案例：SolarWinds 与 xz","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/software-supply-chain-security/foundations/attack-case-studies"},{"seq":3,"slug":"frameworks-slsa","title":"框架：SLSA 与 S2C2F","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/software-supply-chain-security/foundations/frameworks-slsa"}]},{"seq":2,"slug":"dependencies","title":"依赖安全","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/software-supply-chain-security/dependencies","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"dependency-risks","title":"依赖风险：投毒与抢注","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/software-supply-chain-security/dependencies/dependency-risks"},{"seq":2,"slug":"sbom","title":"软件物料清单 SBOM","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/software-supply-chain-security/dependencies/sbom"},{"seq":3,"slug":"vulnerability-scanning","title":"漏洞扫描与 SCA","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/software-supply-chain-security/dependencies/vulnerability-scanning"}]},{"seq":3,"slug":"integrity","title":"完整性","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/software-supply-chain-security/integrity","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"artifact-signing","title":"制品签名：Sigstore","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/software-supply-chain-security/integrity/artifact-signing"},{"seq":2,"slug":"provenance-attestation","title":"来源证明与构建溯源","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/software-supply-chain-security/integrity/provenance-attestation"},{"seq":3,"slug":"reproducible-builds","title":"可重现构建","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/software-supply-chain-security/integrity/reproducible-builds"}]},{"seq":4,"slug":"practices","title":"工程实践","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/software-supply-chain-security/practices","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"secure-pipelines","title":"安全流水线与 CI 加固","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/software-supply-chain-security/practices/secure-pipelines"},{"seq":2,"slug":"policy-enforcement","title":"策略执行与准入控制","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/software-supply-chain-security/practices/policy-enforcement"},{"seq":3,"slug":"incident-response","title":"供应链事件响应","url":"/l-doc-books/h/cs-fundamentals/software-supply-chain-security/practices/incident-response"}]}]}